 {"id": "LORE-015", "title": "README + docs to the fleet's public-deliverable standard (hook headline, real numbers, use-cases)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "phase": "docs", "repo": "https://github.com/get-h3/lore", "detail": "The README ships a hook, the question the tool answers, a runnable walkthrough with REAL numbers from the acceptance replay, and named use-cases. Add CHANGELOG.md and SECURITY.md. Acceptance: someone who has never seen the fleet can run the walkthrough from the README alone.", "reasoning": {"source": "fleet doctrine \u2014 public-facing deliverables are marketing-grade"}, "updated_at": "2026-09-23T21:37:38+00:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/lore-LORE-015", "branch": "wt/LORE-015", "worker_status": "done", "commit_hash": "91f915d", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "Wave worker (worktree wt/LORE-015, glm-5.3-flash @ ollama-cloud): README.md 197L (hook headline, the one-line question, runnable quickstart, named use-cases, design laws, roadmap separating shipped from planned, honest Status), CHANGELOG.md 28L (Keep-a-Changelog, Unreleased, says plainly no tag exists), SECURITY.md 45L (supported versions, GitHub Security Advisories as the private channel, tool-specific threat notes). Foreman independently reproduced EVERY claimed output in the README: 'drain 503' -> gateway-drain-window 0.90; 'secret .env clobber' -> secret-env-clobber 0.90; 'key rotation expired' -> key-rotation-expiry 0.90; coffee-machine -> unclassified; 16 passed. No invented numbers; shipped-vs-planned clearly separated. Tier-1 gitreins PASS 059aedfd.", "foreman_note": "GITREINS TIER-2 VERDICT: PASS/COMPLETE (job-d48cdb5564714dd98075cbc7e7713e9f, verdict c87b88f8 era, judged HEAD c19eacc). The FIRST judge run FAILED this row on a REAL defect it found: README said '16 passed'/'16 tests passing' while the merged tree runs 45 (LORE-004's tests merged in the same wave) plus a Status section listing the then-shipped compiler as unshipped. Fixed foreman-direct in 9a834e4 (re-verified every figure on the merged tree); re-judge returned tier2 COMPLETE with the walkthrough, use-cases, CHANGELOG and SECURITY all verified and every cited number traced to a real command/file/commit. This is a cross-worktree integration defect that only existed AFTER the merge \u2014 the judge caught it on the combined tree."}
